| C2 | **No rate limiting on booking creation** | [bookingService.ts](file:///c:/Users/Nitro%20V15/Documents/GitHub/react-portfolio-2k26/src/services/bookingService.ts) | Same as C1 — bookings can be mass-created with no throttle. |
| C3 | **No honeypot / bot detection on form** | [ProjectInquiryForm.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Nitro%20V15/Documents/GitHub/react-portfolio-2k26/src/components/home/ProjectInquiryForm.tsx) | Zero bot protection. Automated scripts can submit the form trivially. No CAPTCHA, no honeypot field, no timing check. |
| C4 | **Discord webhook URL exposed to client** | [inquiryService.ts](file:///c:/Users/Nitro%20V15/Documents/GitHub/react-portfolio-2k26/src/services/inquiryService.ts#L33) | `VITE_DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` is a `VITE_` prefixed env var, meaning it's **bundled into the frontend JS**. Anyone can extract it and abuse/spam your Discord channel. |
| C5 | **XSS vulnerability in API email templates** | [api/inquiry.ts](file:///c:/Users/Nitro%20V15/Documents/GitHub/react-portfolio-2k26/api/inquiry.ts#L29-L74), [netlify/functions/inquiry.ts](file:///c:/Users/Nitro%20V15/Documents/GitHub/react-portfolio-2k26/netlify/functions/inquiry.ts#L36-L81) | User input (`fullName`, `company`, `description`, `featureChips`) is interpolated directly into HTML email templates with **zero sanitization**. A malicious user can inject `<script>` or HTML into the email. |
| C6 | **No server-side validation in API endpoints** | [api/inquiry.ts](file:///c:/Users/Nitro%20V15/Documents/GitHub/react-portfolio-2k26/api/inquiry.ts), [netlify/functions/inquiry.ts](file:///c:/Users/Nitro%20V15/Documents/GitHub/react-portfolio-2k26/netlify/functions/inquiry.ts) | The serverless functions accept **any** JSON body without validation. No check for required fields, no email format validation, no length limits. |
| C7 | **API email endpoint is completely disconnected** | [inquiryService.ts](file:///c:/Users/Nitro%20V15/Documents/GitHub/react-portfolio-2k26/src/services/inquiryService.ts) | The `submitProjectInquiry` function **never calls** `api/inquiry.ts` or the Netlify function. The email sending code exists as dead code — inquiries are only saved to Supabase, meaning **you never get email notifications** unless the Discord webhook is configured. |
| C8 | **Bookings table has no public SELECT policy** | [00001_init_schema.sql](file:///c:/Users/Nitro%20V15/Documents/GitHub/react-portfolio-2k26/supabase/migrations/00001_init_schema.sql#L104-L129) | The `bookings` table only has `SELECT` for authenticated users. But `bookingService.ts` queries bookings on the public form (line 100-104) to check for booked time slots — **this query silently fails for anonymous users**, returning empty data and showing all slots as available, leading to double-bookings. |
| C9 | **No file type validation on attachments** | [Step3Requirements.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Nitro%20V15/Documents/GitHub/react-portfolio-2k26/src/components/home/inquiry/Step3Requirements.tsx#L41-L68), [inquiryService.ts](file:///c:/Users/Nitro%20V15/Documents/GitHub/react-portfolio-2k26/src/services/inquiryService.ts#L86-L124) | HTML `accept` attribute is easily bypassed. No server-side file type validation. Malicious files (`.exe`, `.bat`) can be uploaded to the public `inquiry-attachments` bucket. |

