### Phase 2: Server-Side Hardening

---

#### [MODIFY] [netlify/functions/inquiry.ts](file:///c:/Users/Nitro%20V15/Documents/GitHub/react-portfolio-2k26/netlify/functions/inquiry.ts)

- **Add server-side validation** — Validate required fields (`fullName`, `email`, `services`, `budget`, `timeline`, `projectType`, `description`). Validate email format. Reject if missing.
- **Add HTML sanitization** — Escape all user input before injecting into the HTML email template (fix C5).
- **Fix HTTP status code** — Change `450` to `405` for Method Not Allowed.
- **Add rate limiting header checks** — Return appropriate `Retry-After` header on rapid requests.
- **Add Discord webhook trigger** — Move the Discord notification here from client-side, using `process.env.DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` (non-`VITE_` prefix so it stays server-side only).

#### [DELETE] [api/inquiry.ts](file:///c:/Users/Nitro%20V15/Documents/GitHub/react-portfolio-2k26/api/inquiry.ts)

- **Remove dead API endpoint** — This Vercel-style handler is never called and duplicates Netlify function logic. Consolidate to the Netlify function only since you deploy on Netlify.

